<nav class="bg-lime-500 shadow">
  <div class="mx-auto max-w-7xl px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 mb-4">
    <%# min-h rather than h: below 640px eight links do not fit on one line, and a fixed
        h-16 clipped the row they wrapped onto instead of growing. Growing alone was not
        enough -- at the desktop type size the wrap ran to three rows and 156px, a quarter
        of a phone screen, above the session a lifter is actually reading. The type is
        smaller on a phone and full size from 640px up, which holds the wrap to two rows
        at its worst -- and since the links took the brand face, which sets about a third
        narrower than the system sans, that worst case is the 640-840px band and the row
        comes back to one from roughly 840px up. %>
    <div class="flex min-h-16 min-w-0 justify-between">
      <%# min-w-0: a flex child will not shrink below its content, so without this the
          scrolling row pushes the whole page sideways instead of scrolling inside itself. %>
      <div class="flex min-w-0">
        <div class="flex flex-nowrap items-center gap-x-5 overflow-x-auto py-2 sm:ml-6 sm:flex-wrap sm:gap-x-8 sm:overflow-x-visible sm:py-0">
        <%# `brand` sits on every link and not once on the row above them, even though
            font-family inherits and one class on the parent would save nine. What was
            wrong here was a face arriving from somewhere else and landing on whatever
            happened to be in its way, so a link that wants the brand face now says so
            itself rather than catching it from a container. The wordmark takes the same
            face as the links beside it: the serif is a display face set at 72px and up on
            the front page, and at the 16px this row runs at on a phone it would be harder
            to read, not more distinguished. What sets the wordmark apart is what already
            did -- darker text and a border that is not transparent. %>
        <a href="/" class="<%= nav_link_style %> text-gray-900">tectonic plates</a>
          <%# The links below are gray-900 at 70%, not the gray-500 they arrived in. That
              grey came from a stock nav that sits on a white bar, where it is 4.83:1 and
              passes AA; this bar is lime-500 and the grey came along unchanged, so it read
              2.45:1 here and hover:text-white took it to 1.98:1 -- pointing at a link made
              it harder to read than leaving it alone. 70% composites over the bar's
              rgb(132, 204, 22) to rgb(52, 78, 34), 4.71:1, and the hover resolves to the
              full gray-900 at 8.98:1, which is toward the wordmark rather than away from
              it. Flat gray-900 at rest clears AA just as well and is one class shorter; it
              was not taken because it hands every link the wordmark's own colour and
              leaves the solid underline to set the wordmark apart on its own. The alpha is
              measured against this bar, so a nav that stops being lime-500 is a nav whose
              links have to be measured again. %>
          <%- if rodauth.logged_in? %>
            <a href="/workouts" class="<%= nav_link_style %> border-transparent text-gray-900/70 hover:border-gray-300 hover:text-gray-900">workouts</a>
            <a href="/exercises" class="<%= nav_link_style %> border-transparent text-gray-900/70 hover:border-gray-300 hover:text-gray-900">exercises</a>
            <a href="/programs" class="<%= nav_link_style %> border-transparent text-gray-900/70 hover:border-gray-300 hover:text-gray-900">programs</a>
            <a href="/volume" class="<%= nav_link_style %> border-transparent text-gray-900/70 hover:border-gray-300 hover:text-gray-900">volume</a>
            <a href="/equipment" class="<%= nav_link_style %> border-transparent text-gray-900/70 hover:border-gray-300 hover:text-gray-900">equipment</a>
            <a href="/connections" class="<%= nav_link_style %> border-transparent text-gray-900/70 hover:border-gray-300 hover:text-gray-900">assistants</a>
            <a href="<%= rodauth.logout_path %>" class="<%= nav_link_style %> border-transparent text-gray-900/70 hover:border-gray-300 hover:text-gray-900">exit</a>
          <%- else %>
            <a href="<%= rodauth.login_path %>" class="<%= nav_link_style %> border-transparent text-gray-900/70 hover:border-gray-300 hover:text-gray-900">log in</a>
            <a href="<%= rodauth.create_account_path %>" class="<%= nav_link_style %> border-transparent text-gray-900/70 hover:border-gray-300 hover:text-gray-900">sign up</a>
          <%- end %>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</nav>
